@lang en
IMPORT `bmfire-insuring-clause`

-- What each party must do, and by when: the warranty in Section IV, Section V, the general
-- conditions (VI), the claims conditions (VII) other than the measures VII.3, VII.5 and
-- VII.6, the premium payment warranty (VIII.3), and the closing note,
-- "GHI CHÚ QUAN TRỌNG".
--
-- TWO KINDS OF RULE. Where the Rules put a duty on a party, with or without a period, it is
-- a regulative rule (`GIVETH A DEONTIC ...`), exercised by `#TRACE` in the tests. Where a
-- duty's breach takes a claim away, the breach is a fact on the claim file and there is a
-- boolean the claim module reads.
--
-- THE CONDITIONS ARE CONDITIONS PRECEDENT. The preamble says the conditions of the Rules
-- "được coi là điều kiện tiên quyết đối với quyền đòi bồi thường" (are deemed conditions
-- precedent to the right to claim). So a condition the Insured did not meet takes the
-- claim away whether or not the failure caused or worsened the loss (fork F29; the Law on
-- Insurance Business, art. 46, limits what an insurer may do for late notice: LAW).
--
-- CLOCKS. The deontic rules count in days, except VII.8 (arbitration) and the two
-- twelve-month bars of VII.2(b), which the Rules state in months; VII.8's rule counts in
-- months and says so. Date functions use calendar days and `add months`.

§ `Conditions and duties`

§§ `The parties and their acts`

DECLARE `A party to the policy` IS ONE OF
    `Bao Minh`
    `the Insured`
    `the arbitrators`

DECLARE `An act under the policy` IS ONE OF
    `disclose truthfully and fully every fact the Insured knows or could know`
    `insure the deductible`
    `keep the insured property in good repair and take every proper measure to prevent DAMAGE`
    `send notice of cancellation by registered letter to the Insured's last known address`
    `refund the premium for the period no longer insured`
    `give notice of termination`
    `take steps to minimise the loss and recover lost property`
    `notify Bao Minh in writing`
    `notify the police`
    `deliver the written claim, with particulars of any other insurance`
    `supply the information and documents Bao Minh reasonably requires, with a sworn statement`
    `supply the plans, documents, quantities and dimensions needed to repair or replace`
    `enter the scene to assess the loss, or take over the building`
    `take over insured property, or require it to be handed over`
    `act to enforce rights against third parties, at Bao Minh's expense`
    `agree a sole arbitrator in writing`
    `appoint an arbitrator in writing`
    `appoint a sole arbitrator in writing`
    `appoint an umpire in writing`
    `pay the premium in full`

§§ `Closing note — disclosure`

-- The Insured must tell the insurer, truthfully and fully, everything it knows or could
-- know, so as not to lose the right to be paid. The note names no period: it is a duty
-- of the proposal, standing until performed. Its sanction is VI.2.
