§§ `VII.8 — arbitration`

-- A dispute about the AMOUNT to be paid goes to one arbitrator the parties appoint in
-- writing; if they cannot agree one, to two, one appointed in writing by each,
-- "sau hai tháng" (after two months) from a party's receipt of the other's written request to
-- choose. If a party fails to appoint within two months of receiving the other's written
-- notice, the other may appoint a sole arbitrator. Two arbitrators who cannot agree
-- appoint an umpire in writing. The arbitrators decide the costs and the amount.
-- A dispute about LIABILITY is not within this condition; it goes to suit (VII.2(b)(i)).
